1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,500
Every student in a Class 8 classroom

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:09,200
is at a different place in the same chapter.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:15,000
LearnWise AI adapts to where each one actually is
and shows the teacher what that looks like.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,500
A fixed lesson moves on at one speed,

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:26,000
whether or not the student is ready.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Adaptive learning picks the next question
from the answers just given.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
In this prototype those choices come from
written rules — not a black box.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,500
This is Aarav, a sample Class 8 student —
not a real child.

9
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:45,000
His dashboard shows points, a streak, his level,

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
and one recommended next step.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The “why this?” panel shows the rule behind it.

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,500
Eight questions on fractions,
variables and equations.

13
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:05,000
I will answer the fraction questions
wrong on purpose,

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,500
to show what happens next.

15
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:14,000
Nothing here is timed.

16
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The score comes only from the answers
I actually chose.

17
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Three of eight correct.

18
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,500
Fractions is flagged as the gap, with the evidence.

19
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:35,000
Practice starts there, and every answer shows
why the next question was chosen.

20
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
The tutor explains the same idea with a pizza:

21
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
why 1/2 + 1/3 is 5/6 — not 2/5.

22
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The path enforces prerequisites.

23
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,500
Fractions is below 60 percent,

24
00:01:55,500 --> 00:02:00,000
so later topics stay locked, and say why.

25
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,000
That is how a gap gets closed, not carried forward.

26
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:11,000
The teacher sees the same evidence at class level:

27
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:16,000
strengths, students who need support,
common misconceptions.

28
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Aarav's row shows a dash where he has not answered,

29
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,500
so missing work is never counted as failure.

30
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:30,000
Plans are labelled suggestions — the teacher decides.

31
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,000
The language switch changes the interface
and the teaching text.

32
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,000
The coverage table states which topics are translated.

33
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Low-data mode trims animation. Saved lessons read
offline — live tutoring does not.

34
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:50,000
LearnWise AI helps every student learn
at their own pace,

35
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:55,000
while giving teachers better insight
into how to support them.

36
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Rules over real answers, three languages,
an honest label on everything simulated. Code Kernel '26.
